    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9659b0abe753468f92605285366b4389",
      "statement": "One MCP tool call runs the shared scalar boundary rather than MCP-specific logic: FastMCP coerces JSON into tool_fn's keyword arguments, tool_fn hands them as a payload dict to the packed run callable (scalar_executor.extract_executor_fn), which validates the payload into the input DTO — running ValueObject validate_fn on wire input — executes it through UseFramework.__call__ (middleware, context, tracing, error handlers unchanged), and dumps the response as a JSON-safe dict.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/mcp/mcp.py#L27-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:83a8095156f4d71c02ddd93703c4d3e5ec2e83c6dce2436dbcd710a33dc5a50b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/scalar_executor.py#L21-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9195ae6d0e8ba4eefb7a2120a3c87726bb72bda71308315b12c72412bdd35204:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/scalar_executor.py#L57-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:56bbf29a0bd27bc179a81540d5dc968a96e81849b62be7ecfc876ab05467db91:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4665d3aff8564b1a8dcc0dcf4dcf53d3",
      "statement": "Transport is the only difference between deployments: Entrypoint.run(name=None, **kwargs) is self.server(name=name).run(**kwargs), so omitting transport starts the stdio host used by desktop MCP clients, transport='http' serves MCP Streamable HTTP at /mcp (still MCP tools/list and tools/call, not a REST/OpenAPI API), and all other keywords (host, port, path, ...) pass through to FastMCP unchanged.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/entrypoint_mcp.md#L242-L252",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cda28cce1d46dc168b2dfd25346159a3fbea91c1973149d6f9dcde0eca14331a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/mcp/entrypoint.py#L64-L71",
